🚀 How to Run and Verify the Upgrades
Since Docker Desktop is currently installing/updating on your system, please perform the following verification steps once it has finished launching:

Step 1: Start the Cluster with 3 Replicas
Run this command in the workspace directory to build and boot the cluster:

powershell

docker compose up -d --build --scale app=3
Step 2: Access the Dashboard
Open your browser and navigate to:


http://localhost:8080
It will automatically redirect you to the secure dashboard on https://localhost:8443 (accept the browser's local self-signed certificate warning to proceed).

Step 3: Verify Load Balancing (Round Robin / Least Conn)
On the dashboard, click "Send Request" multiple times.
Observe the Active Node Replica badge change colors and show different container IDs.
Check the Recent Request Log to see requests distributed across different replicas.
Step 4: Scale the Cluster Dynamically
Scale up to 5 replicas dynamically without restarting Nginx:

powershell

docker compose up -d --scale app=5
Step 5: Test Sticky Sessions (Session Persistence)
Open 
nginx.conf
.
Comment out least_conn; (line 22) and uncomment # ip_hash; (line 23).
Reload Nginx dynamically:
powershell

docker compose exec nginx nginx -s reload
Click "Send Request" in the browser. You will notice the serving container ID remains static (sticky) for your session.
